# UX Principles

## Navigation

Two tabs only: **Trips** and **Me**. Do not add Weather, Assistant, Explore, Discover, Tools, Packing, or Profile tabs. Weather, Ask PackWise, Final Check, and destination notes live inside a trip.

## First launch

Value in seconds. No signup, no notification permission, no location permission, no subscription wall.

1. Welcome — “Pack what this trip actually needs.” CTA **Get Started**
2. One trip can be many things — composable trip types, activities, and bags
3. Your choices stay yours — CTA **Create My First Trip**

All three pages share one shell. Do not claim memory-driven personalization before that product ships.

## Trips home

Extremely clean. Upcoming card: destination, dates, trip-scoped weather, `31 of 42 packed`, items left. Later trips: quiet “Packing list ready”. Past: Completed. Main CTA **+ New Trip**.

## Trip setup

Progressive steps, not one form. V1: one primary destination.

1. Destination — MapKit search, store displayName/city/region/country/coords/timeZone
2. Dates — native range; persist **days and nights**
3. Travelers — single party mode: Just me / Me + partner / Family / Group
4. Trip types — **multi-select** Vacation, City Break, Beach, Business, Outdoor, Road Trip, Wedding/Event, Ski/Snow, Festival, Visiting Family, Other. No primary type
5. Activities — multi-select type-based chips + **+ Add something** free text
6. Bags — **multi-select** Personal item / Carry-on / Checked / Backpack. Empty means Not sure/no constraint. Road Trip is not a bag
7. Style + laundry — both separate single-select policies; Light / **Balanced (default)** / Prepared and No laundry / If needed / Planned
8. About you — multi-select chips + free note
9. Review

Every step uses native Back/cancel, progress, title/helper/content, and a sticky bottom primary action. Do not put Next at top-right.

Review → **Build My Packing List**. Short real wait copy only. Never “AI is generating”.

Natural-language “Tell PackWise about your trip” is V1.1, not MVP.

## Packing list

Trip Detail is the core screen. Packing dominates. Categories: Essentials, Documents, Clothing, Footwear, Toiletries, Electronics, Health, Activities, Travel Comfort, Miscellaneous.

Rows like Apple Reminders. Cards only for Packing Impact, Weather Changed, Final Check, packing suggestions.

```text
○ T-shirts ×4
○ Rain jacket
    Rain expected Saturday
```

Swipe left: Delete / Not Needed. Swipe right: Pack. Long press: Edit, move, quantity, Why this item?, Don't suggest on trips like this.

Item sheet: why + Recommended by (Forecast, Activities — never AI/GPT/Algorithm).

Always show quantities. Explain on tap. Deduplicate overlapping footwear/layers internally.

Solo filters: To pack / Packed / Important. Party lists add a compact People scope (All / stable traveler labels / Shared). In party All, group identical canonical personal items for presentation; traveler filters show real records.

Progress: `31 of 42 packed` + items left. Near departure: `4 essentials still unpacked`.

## Weather

Trip dates only. Not a general weather app. Faraway trips: honest “forecast isn’t available yet” + seasonal list. When a packing signal changes after generation: **Weather changed** card, then the same review sheet as edit-trip. Additions default on; removals default off. **User always controls the list.** No M4 weather notifications in this slice.

Packing Impact is the brand differentiator (rain → jacket, cool evenings → layer, hiking → trail shoes).

## Lifecycle

Phases are automatic: list ready → forecast ready → 3 days → day before → **Final Check** on departure. During trip: get out of the way, not itinerary mode. Post-trip: max 5 questions.

Notifications must be useful. Never “PackWise misses you” or “It’s packing time! 🎉”.

Share MVP: native share sheet of the formatted list.

## Me

Show human habits (“You usually bring”, “You tend to skip”), not raw stats. Preferences: default style/bag, units, workout, laptop, contacts, medication. Do not collect passport numbers or medical records.

